        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1933fa61-aa3e-57cb-9b36-2f76ee22d5db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Entabeni Game Reserve\n- Animals: South African cheetah, Transvaal lion, African bush elephant, South African giraffe, African leopard, warthog, African buffalo, hippopotamus\n- Concepts: IUCN conservation status\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1986, the South African cheetah has been classified as Vulnerable by the IUCN.\n- The South African cheetah, also known as the Namibian cheetah and scientifically named Acinonyx jubatus jubatus, is the most numerous and nominate cheetah subspecies native to Southern Africa.\n- Entabeni Game Reserve is home to the South African cheetah and other safari animals including the Transvaal lion, African bush elephant, South African giraffe, African leopard, warthog, African buffalo, and hippopotamus.\n- Entabeni Game Reserve contains a variety of habitats for these safari animals.",
